-- lib/match.cub — first-order matching and rewriting over codes. Loaded after lib/code.cub.
-- The one operation behind the specializer's rewriting along marked theorems (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.6 “B15 — The specializer”,
-- “Steps, in order”, step 3 “Rewrite”) and the navigation layer's "available transports" (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.14 “F33 — Navigation: the concrete form”): given an identity whose left
-- side is a pattern, find every position in a term where the pattern matches, and replace it by
-- the right side under the match. A pattern is a code whose variables above a bound are
-- metavariables; matching binds them; the match is a list of (metavariable, code).
-- Variables are de Bruijn indices (code.cub). A pattern with k bound variables (its own λs,
-- counted from the outside) uses cvar n with n ≥ k as metavariables m = n − k. A metavariable
-- that occurs under b binders of the pattern binds a subterm that is then shifted by b when
-- instantiated under different binders.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- codes: shifting
-- cmap f d c: c with each subterm p at binder depth d replaced by f p d where f gives one, every
-- constructor of Code traversed (the leaves have no variables); the one traversal every
-- index-changing operation below is defined by, so none can skip a construct
cmap f d c =
  case f c d of
    some c2 → c2
    none → cmap-in f d c
